  "why_scout_cares": "A film recorder that makes a computer's graphics real by exposing one sheet of instant film three times — once each through red, green, and blue filters — so the colour never has to exist as display phosphors, but as light colour-mixed on a chemical substrate you peel apart. The interaction is a physical, mechanical ritual of colour separation, the polar opposite of a monitor. Museum's only computer-to-photographic-film output, distinct from every display and print exhibit.",
